# Real libc abs body: a short branchless sequence with 1-cycle ALU ops.
# Each 1.00 below is the latency column for its ALU row: mov, neg, and ret.
# REQUIRES: x86_64, system-libc
# RUN: perf analyze /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6:abs -e index,assembly,latency 2>&1 | %FileCheck %s
# CHECK-NOT: Traceback
# CHECK: index assembly latency
# CHECK-NEXT: endbr64
# CHECK: mov eax, edi 1.00
# CHECK: neg eax 1.00
# CHECK: ret 0.00
# CHECK-NOT: Traceback
